2.1 The Provider shall provide to the Client the following bookkeeping services (the "Services"):

(a) Monthly processing of income and expenditure transactions, including sales receipts, supplier invoices, and bank transactions;

(b) Reconciliation of the Client's bank accounts, credit card accounts, and petty cash on a monthly basis, to be completed no later than the fifteenth (15th) Business Day following the end of each calendar month;

(c) Preparation and submission of VAT returns (MTD-compliant) to HMRC on a quarterly basis, including the maintenance of all digital records required under the Making Tax Digital regime;

(d) Maintenance of the Client's sales ledger and purchase ledger, including the raising of sales invoices where instructed by the Client and the chasing of overdue accounts where specifically requested;

(e) Preparation of monthly management accounts, comprising a profit and loss account, balance sheet, and cash flow summary, to be delivered to the Client by the twentieth (20th) Business Day following the end of each calendar month;

(f) Processing of payroll for up to six (6) employees, including RTI submissions to HMRC and pension scheme administration;

(g) Preparation of the annual accounts file for onward transmission to the Client's appointed accountant;

(h) Ad hoc bookkeeping support by email or telephone during normal business hours, not exceeding three (3) hours per calendar month in aggregate.

2.2 The Services do not include:

(a) The preparation of statutory accounts or corporation tax returns, which shall remain the responsibility of the Client's appointed accountant;

(b) The provision of audit or assurance services;

(c) Legal, tax, or financial advice beyond the scope of routine bookkeeping queries;

(d) The correction of errors in records that predate the Effective Date, unless separately agreed in writing.

2.3 The Client shall provide the Provider with access to all relevant records, documentation, and accounting software credentials necessary for the performance of the Services. Such access shall be provided on or before the third (3rd) Business Day of each calendar month.

